#doc (Manual) "{tight}[Modular forms modulo $`p`]" =>
%%%
tag := "modular-forms-modulo-p"
htmlSplit := .never
%%%

# The definition
%%%
tag := "modp-definition"
%%%

Let $`k \in \mathbb{Z}`. A power series $`f \in \mathbb{F}_p\llbracket X\rrbracket` is a
_mod-$`p` modular form of weight $`k`_ if it is the reduction modulo $`p` of a $`p`-integral
modular form of weight $`k`. We denote by $`M_k(\mathbb{F}_p)` the $`\mathbb{F}_p`-submodule of
$`\mathbb{F}_p\llbracket X\rrbracket` of mod-$`p` modular forms of weight $`k`.

{docstring PowerSeries.isModPModularForm}

{docstring modPModularForms}

We denote by {name EisensteinSeries.E₂ModP}`E₂ModP`, {name EisensteinSeries.E₄ModP}`E₄ModP` and
{name EisensteinSeries.E₆ModP}`E₆ModP` the reductions of $`E_2`, $`E_4` and $`E_6`. For
$`p \geq 5` we have $`E_2 \in M_{p+1}(\mathbb{F}_p)`
({name EisensteinSeries.E₂ModP_mem_modPModularForms}`E₂ModP_mem_modPModularForms`).

# Evaluation modulo $`p`
%%%
tag := "evaluation-modulo-p"
%%%

We define the $`\mathbb{F}_p`-algebra homomorphism
$`\mathbb{F}_p[X_0, X_1] \to \mathbb{F}_p\llbracket X\rrbracket` sending $`X_0` to $`E_4` and
$`X_1` to $`E_6`, and its restriction to $`\mathbb{F}_p[X_0, X_1]_n`. Both take values in
$`\mathbb{F}_p\llbracket X\rrbracket`. We write $`\operatorname{ev}` for
{name ModularForm.evalE₄E₆ModP}`evalE₄E₆ModP`.

{docstring ModularForm.evalE₄E₆ModP}

{docstring ModularForm.evalE₄E₆ModPAtWeight}

Let $`p \geq 5` and $`n \in \mathbb{N}`. The restriction of $`\operatorname{ev}` to
$`\mathbb{F}_p[X_0, X_1]_n` is injective, and every element of $`M_n(\mathbb{F}_p)` is
$`\operatorname{ev}(F)` for some $`F \in \mathbb{F}_p[X_0, X_1]_n`.

{docstring ModularForm.evalE₄E₆ModPAtWeight_injective}

{docstring ModularForm.exists_isWeightedHomogeneous_of_mem_modPModularForms}

No graded algebra of mod-$`p` modular forms is defined.

# The Hasse invariant
%%%
tag := "hasse-invariant"
%%%

Let $`p \geq 5`. By {ref "pint-evaluation-discriminant"}[the structure theorem over
$`\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}`] there is a unique $`\tilde A \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[X_0, X_1]_{p-1}` whose
evaluation at $`E_4`, $`E_6` is $`E_{p-1}`. We define the _Hasse invariant_
$`A \in \mathbb{F}_p[X_0, X_1]` as the reduction of $`\tilde A` modulo $`p`. It is a polynomial,
not a modular form.

{docstring ModularForm.hasseInvPoly}

Here {name EisensteinSeries.ModP.E}`ModP.E` is {name EisensteinSeries.E_int}`E_int` in weight
$`p - 1`.

Let $`p \geq 5`. Then $`\operatorname{ev}(A) = 1`.

{docstring ModularForm.evalE₄E₆ModP_hasseInvPoly}

Let $`p \geq 5`. The kernel of $`\operatorname{ev}` is the ideal generated by $`A - 1`
{citep swinnertonDyer73}[]. Moreover $`A - 1` is irreducible and $`A` is squarefree.

{docstring ModularForm.ker_evalE₄E₆ModP}

{docstring ModularForm.irreducible_hasseInvPoly_sub_one}

{docstring ModularForm.hasseInvPoly_squarefree}
